 FCA's number for this recall is VA6.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":11463,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V680000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":8,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2013","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2011","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2012","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2015","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2017","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2016","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V524000","received":"2018-08-09","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:WIRING:FRONT UNDERHOOD","summary":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC) is recalling certain 2018 Jeep Renegade, Compass and Grand Cherokee, RAM 1500 and Promaster, Fiat 500x, Dodge Journey, Challenger, Charger and Durango and Chrysler 300x vehicles, 2017-2018 Jeep Wrangler, Dodge Grand Caravan and Chrysler Town and Country vehicles and 2018-2019 Jeep Cherokee and 2018 Chrysler Pacifica and Pacifica Hybrid vehicles.  The powertrain control module may be equipped with a voltage regulator chip in the circuit board that may fail, causing a stall or a no start condition.","consequence":"A vehicle stall can increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will replace the powertrain control module, free of charge.  The recall began October 2, 2018.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is U87.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":12779,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V524000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":23,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2018","make":"FIAT","model":"500X"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"PACIFICA"},{"year":"2018","make":"DODGE","model":"DURANGO"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"PACIFICA"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"CHEROKEE"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"},{"year":"2017","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"},{"year":"2018","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"},{"year":"2018","make":"DODGE","model":"CHALLENGER"},{"year":"2018","make":"DODGE","model":"JOURNEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"JEEP","model":"CHEROKEE"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"RENEGADE"},{"year":"2018","make":"RAM","model":"PROMASTER"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"COMPASS"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"GRAND CHEROKEE"},{"year":"2018","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2018","make":"RAM","model":"1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"PACIFICA PLUG-IN HYBRID"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"PACIFICA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"16V849000","received":"2016-11-23","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:STORAGE:TANK ASSEMBLY","summary":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC) is recalling certain model year 2017 Jeep Wrangler vehicles manufactured November 1, 2016, to November 3, 2016.  The affected vehicles may have a fuel tank that has a cracked or broken control valve, possibly resulting in a fuel leak in a rollover event, debris in the fuel tank and/or the potential of over fueling the vehicle.","consequence":"A fuel leak in the presence of an ignition source can increase the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and Jeep dealers will inspect the fuel tank and replace fuel tank and sending unit, as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began January 12, 2017.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is S90.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":359,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=16V849000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":1,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"16V734000","received":"2016-10-13","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"AIR BAGS:FRONTAL:SENSOR/CONTROL MODULE-INACTIVE","summary":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC) is recalling certain model year 2016-2017 Jeep Wrangler vehicles manufactured June 16, 2015, to August 14, 2016.  In certain crash conditions, the front impact sensor wiring may be pulled until it detaches before a signal can be received by the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC).","consequence":"If the ORC module does not receive a signal from the front impact sensor, both frontal air bags and the seat belt pretensioners will not deploy in the event of a crash, increasing the risk of injury.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will reroute the front impact sensor wiring and relocate the impact sensor branch, free of charge.  The recall began on November 10, 2016.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is S76.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":182743,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=16V734000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2016","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V098000","received":"2018-02-08","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"EXTERIOR LIGHTING:BRAKE LIGHTS:SWITCH","summary":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC) is recalling certain 2017 Dodge Caravan and Jeep Wrangler vehicles.  The brake switches on these vehicles may malfunction, keeping the brake lights illuminated and/or allowing the vehicle to be shifted out of the PARK position without the brake pedal being pushed.","consequence":"Having the brake lamps continuously illuminated or being able to shift the vehicle out of PARK when the brake pedal is not\r\npressed (and the ignition is in the RUN mode) can increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will replace the brake switches, free of charge.  The recall began March 22, 2018.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is U09.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":39456,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V098000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2017","make":"DODGE","model":"CARAVAN"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
